  body = "Keep small TCG invalidation page-lock sets in four caller-owned sorted\nentries. Create the tree only on the fifth distinct existing page and\ntransfer held and busy state into stable heap entries without releasing\nlocks. Retain discovery acquisition order, ascending retry and release,\nopposite-page deduplication, and precise-SMC cleanup before nonlocal exit.\n\nRetain versioned process control, exact virtual coordinates, independent\nchild resources, canonical guest-state projection and complete matching\nsource integration. Preserve stopped-owner generations, registered reader\nand callback custody, FIFO barriers, fault settlement and descriptor\nfailure refusal across snapshot, restore and retained fork operations.\n\nPreserve accelerator instance classification, cold continuation checks,\nempty fault-queue admission, active instruction-context observation,\ndirect register-rule presence, cached tick-mode admission and native\nmutex owner identity. Keep tracked waiter updates under the existing\nregistry guard, with unsigned wrap, underflow refusal, condition waiter\nidentity and retained fork transaction ordering unchanged.\n\nKeep ordinary RR event ordering and Sim flush fixed points. Preserve all\nguest accesses, invalidation ranges, PageDesc and TB membership, dirty\naccounting, callback order, replay clock observations and scheduling.\n\nExercise actual page collection, native fast invalidation, locked range\nhandling and native page removal with explicit providers. Compare exact\nbaseline lock traces for zero, missing, duplicate, boundary and spilled\nsets, including busy trylocks and precise-SMC nonlocal cleanup. Carry\ncausal controls for omitted pages, lost spill state, missing cleanup,\nreversed iteration, absent first-page admission and eager tree creation.\n\nExtend the system-mode x86 SMC regression with a shared first physical\npage and five distinct second pages, patches through both memberships,\nspilled current-TB cleanup and restored temporary mappings. Retain the\nstrict public prototypes and compiler macros in the native waiter proof.\n\nStrict source-built syntax checks pass for the prototype, baseline and\nall six mutations. The inline collection remains a prototype pending\nconfigured native execution, guest, replay and performance qualification.\n\nKeep a page-locked derived count of recorded TB memberships requiring a\nsecond distinct physical page. Skip only the preliminary lock-discovery\nwalk when that count is zero after acquiring the page lock. Preserve\nnonzero and unknown traversal, retry ordering and actual invalidation.\nSaturate at UINT32_MAX, retain unknown until the list is empty or fully\ncleared, and update only insertion, successful tagged unlink and full flush.\nKeep physical aliases at zero and invalid retained memberships counted.\n\nExtract native insertion, duplicate-QHT rollback, hash invalidation and\nrecursive list-clear bodies into focused proofs. Verify both list tags,\nmixed lists, final crossing removal, sticky saturation, empty and flush\nrecovery, retry after a competing membership change, precise-SMC cleanup\nand retained process fork copies. Strict source-built compilation and\nexecution pass. Seven causal controls fail runtime native assertions;\nsealed-baseline collection stdout matches exactly. Guest SMC, MTTCG,\nreplay and performance remain unqualified for this prototype.\n\nPlace the crossing count directly after QemuSpin, before the tagged list\nhead. The extracted native QemuSpin and PageDesc definitions measured with\nthe source-built 64-bit compiler retain the baseline 16-byte descriptor,\nusing the existing four-byte padding rather than enlarging it to 24 bytes.\nThis layout probe is not a full configured QEMU compilation. The same nine\nfocused proof cases pass after the layout correction.\n\nRetain a thread-private validated search position for x86 TSC sources.\nResolve it against current array storage and compare the complete source\nkind and instance on every hit; keep original scans for misses and all\nother clock kinds. Remain useful before binding or manifest finalization\nwithout caching pointers, absent results, activation, values or time.\nPreserve live guards, transform evidence, replay and clock-read ordering.\n\nExercise production lookup, manifest sorting, activation and projection\nbodies with real GLib arrays, native fork and a cold replacement thread.\nCompare sealed-reference traces and quiescent relocation, sorting, exact\nkeys, live restore guards, values and terminal refusal. Nine compiled\ncausal controls fail native assertions. Preserve the existing exhaustive\ncold fault proof with the original clock-kind enum in its test adapter.\nRegistry mutation providers remain quiescent; guest, migration-stream,\nretained-runtime and performance qualification remain outstanding.\n\nEmit the native unsealed second-lookup row count on stderr after its\nassertion. Retain five identical lifecycle stdout observations and all\nproduction functions. Strict proofs retain candidate one-row lookup,\nreference five-row lookup and nine native assertion controls.\n\nAdd opt-in native node command and stop callbacks on the GPL-side plugin\ninterface. Preserve legacy dispatch when no native control is registered.\nBind immutable command sequences and digests; refuse settlement and nonzero\nphase or microstep requests rather than substituting legacy execution.\n\nClamp RR retirement to an exclusive native ceiling using absolute 50 ps\ninstruction service. Administrative parks retain the next retirement deadline\nand partial service credit across command partitions without rebasing time.\nKeep virtual timers, including AioContext lists, behind the native RR owner;\nwithhold modeled work while no command is admitted or after a stop receipt.\n\nExtend the resource manifest with the V4 native control descriptor, callback,\nworker and prepared-scope identity. Validate the connected Unix datagram fd\nand retain its device/inode identity. Keep native inventory incomplete and\nrefuse capture, restore and hot fork while command-journal custody remains\nunqualified; reject legacy time advancement under native registration.\n\nCarry service-clock VMState scalars and hostile-state validation without\nclaiming complete native state support. Stop receipts expose native deadlines\nand service credit with unknown pending-source inventory. Idle transitions,\ndevice/input/output closure, settlement and full native profiles remain\nunsupported. Add arithmetic and real-QEMU ceiling and partition fixtures.\n\nDiagnostic source builds for x86_64 and aarch64 and actual x86 exclusive-ceiling\nand partition probes passed. Their binaries retain the old package identity;\nthese diagnostics establish neither packaged qualification nor distribution.\n\nRetain original PIT timer arms with native generations, FIFO order and\nexclusive timing horizons. Emit scoped CPU park and timer facts without\nclaiming complete interrupt, deferred-work, input or device closure. Preserve\nthe next service deadline and genuine original timer arms across partitions.\n\nAdd private KVM clock component negotiation and QMP control while refusing\nunsupported acceleration and unqualified complete node profiles. Native\nx86_64 and aarch64 source builds and existing Aio, icount and vCPU service\nregressions pass; live x86 CPU/timer probes preserve original custody.\nThis component stage does not qualify complete native capture or forks.\n\nRetain a genuine asynchronous native writer HOLD through the original\nRR owner instead of permitting broad event-loop release. The held query\nbinds scope, original command, generation and bounded native CPU, work,\nBH, Aio and handler inventories. A wrong scope or insufficient capacity\nrefuses without releasing or replacing original writer custody.\n\nKeep pointer-bearing native rows local to the GPL process; portable\nobservations contain only checked scalar identities and process-neutral\ncoordinates. Preserve legacy execution when native control is disabled.\n\nNative x86 and ARM builds, 33 Aio tests, icount/service regressions and\nexclusive CPU/PIT partition probes pass. CPU/IRQ future producers,\nplugin journals, input/output payloads and complete device state remain\nunqualified; this stage does not enable native capture or fork.\n\nRetain the first unknown native CPU-work, interrupt or reset source diagnostic under the original prepared scope. Preserve actual queued work and expose immutable unknown-birth/effects facts without waiting for BQL or claiming physical containment. Invalidate fresh execution and stop evidence after the source fault; require independent supervisor containment. Bound original native run-owner scalar history.\n\nAdd opt-in original construction epochs and bounded native HOME processing\nunder the pinned initialization scope. Retain original pending callbacks,\nwriter generations and immutable cuts until matching acknowledgement. Keep\nordinary execution closed before acknowledgement and preserve the existing\nV4 command, FIFO and absolute instruction-service semantics.\n\nAdd separately negotiated KVM kernel edition three with its exact component\nbitmap and disjoint QMP namespace. Retain edition one behavior and refuse\nunsupported acceleration, device absence and complete profile qualification.\nKeep the userspace exit, device/input and whole-domain closure gaps explicit.\n\nPreserve the production CPU reset-ingress guard while providing its existing\nno-CPU unit link target with a queue-checked stub. No native source file is\nadded or removed, and every original source license remains unchanged.\n\nCombined x86_64 and aarch64 configured default builds pass, together with\n46 native unit cases, both initial-argument refusal suites, actual KVM\ncomponent refusal cases and extracted-production ABI/error checks. The\nactual host/plugin/native initialization probe and four V4 native control\nregressions pass against the combined sources. These component results do\nnot qualify complete native readiness, phase/input closure, snapshots,\nretained forks, or actual KVM execution on a host lacking the device.\n\nUpdate the existing extracted native regression adapters for the admitted\ninitialization, original timer, CPU fault and native writer identities.\nKeep production implementation files and public legacy layouts unchanged.\nMake absolute instruction-service probes assert the original 50 ps clock\nand explicitly refuse legacy warp or restart under native registration.\n\nNineteen extracted production proofs and eleven compiled executable\nmutation controls pass. The complete configured default builds pass for\nx86_64 and aarch64, together with forty-six native unit cases and actual\nQMP edition-one/edition-three refusal and malformed-edition probes. These\nfixture corrections do not qualify complete native readiness or KVM\nexecution without the accelerator device.\n\nAdd an independently negotiated native phase-control component with bounded\noriginal virtual timer arm inventories, immutable retained cut identity and\nlate authentic CPU coordinate sampling. Preserve the legacy command and\nobservation layouts, conservative refusal and original 50 ps instruction\nservice. Do not grant execution or capture authority from a timer inventory.\n\nPark enrolled native preparation on a dedicated event with the BQL released.\nService only the original pinned finite HOME callbacks before ordinary main\nloop polling. Retain matching original cuts and pending writer rows through\nacknowledgment; reject registration outside BQL ownership and preserve the\nno-initializer path. Install the virtual timer owner at the successful late\nphase seam when CPU construction precedes plugin installation.\n\nConfigured x86_64 and aarch64 source builds and native units pass. Actual\nexclusive PIT instruction cuts, malformed phase-query controls, sixteen\nrepeated original three-callback HOME runs and legacy V4 controls pass.\nThese components do not qualify complete native phase closure, IRQ/device\nsettlement, snapshots, retained forks or a complete simulation node.\n\nAdd an independently opted-in finite original KVM userspace exit ledger.\nBind the kernel vCPU identity once before creation, retain original IO/MMIO\ncallback and response custody through genuine successful kernel reentry,\nand preserve sticky uncertainty after interrupted or failed reentry.\nReserve transition credit before native RUN, reject CPU slot replacement\nand register writes beneath unresolved responses, and expose only bounded\nread-only observations while actual CPU threads are acknowledged paused.\n\nPreserve the original edition-one and edition-three clock/QAPI contracts.\nKeep device, DMA, input, output and whole-profile qualification false.\nNo native source file is added or removed; original licenses remain intact.\n\nConfigured two-ISA native builds, forty-six native unit cases, fifteen\nextracted ledger controls and nine compiled executable mutation controls\npass. Current aggregate source verification preserves all unchanged files,\nand nineteen existing extracted proofs and the mandatory source predicates\npass. Both ISA command-refusal suites pass without a KVM device. These\ncomponent checks do not qualify live hardware execution or native snapshots.\n\nRetain the original post-initialization preparation observation as a bounded,\nimmutable source object. Encode the Applied receipt, CPU park, writer inventory\nand timer births explicitly in big-endian form, compare two native observations,\nand publish the original bytes with release/acquire ordering. Chunk readers\nauthenticate the original scope, sequence and content digest and never resample\nlater execution state. Creation requires the original RR/BQL hold before any\nexecution command; cached observations grant neither acknowledgment nor Ready.\n\nRetain separately opted-in finite original timer selections and their first\ndequeued, cancelled or rearmed disposition. Distinguish replacement births\nfrom the original selected identity and generation; refuse changed original\nHOLD observations before copying cached data. Keep unknown roots and ordering\nexplicit and grant no phase execution permission from these observations.\n\nEnroll native administrative readers using genuine inherited Unix datagram\nsocket identity, operating-system thread identity and thread-local ownership.\nPreserve the edition-six manifest prefix while adding bounded edition-seven\nrole facts. Refuse foreign threads, forked readers and descriptor replacement;\nretain unknown worker roots and the complete original worker bitmap.\n\nAdd separately opted-in completion-only KVM response handling with bounded\noriginal callback response geometry, exact retry and immutable exit identity.\nPreserve sticky uncertainty across interrupted responses and refuse register\nstate writes beneath unresolved callbacks. Dispatch remains closed without\nexclusive genuine CPU callback custody; no live KVM hardware qualification\nis claimed on a host without the accelerator device.\n\nConfigured default builds for both ISAs, existing source proofs, native\ncompatibility probes and compiled negative mutations pass for these\ncomponents. These mechanisms do not authorize full native readiness,\nwhole-world phase closure, exact capture or device-profile qualification.\n\nRetain exclusive original KVM service work and callback lifetime.\n\nA finite CPU service slot keeps the original work off ordinary drain paths and\nrefuses other CPU runs before consumption. Response completion registers its\nactual owner while the device callback can release the BQL, and a global guard\nserializes clock mutations with that lifetime. Ambiguous completion fences the\noriginal request; it does not redispatch the device callback.\n\nThese opt-in source mechanisms preserve disabled-profile behavior and older\nclock/control protocol encodings. They do not establish whole-device readiness,\natomic quantum admission, input/output closure or exact continuation. Hardware\nKVM qualification remains required.\n\nRetain original fixed microvm constructor lifetimes.\n\nBind the original native device and bus roster to real constructor handles,\nstrong object references, parentage and complete QOM census. Retain every\nallocated timer, including dormant migration and clock timers, with its\noriginal callback, payload, list, generation and scale. Refuse unsupported\nlifetime replacement and dormant activation before native mutation.\n\nRetain the actual single BIOS loader backing and complete read-only FW_CFG\nbuffers, native file order, cursor, DMA and property state. Authenticate\noriginal loaded bytes without treating mutable firmware RAM as immutable.\nThe late VAPIC advertisement does not imply a second loaded option ROM.\n\nCompare the complete original root policy and version-eight manifest while\npreserving older manifest prefixes. Explicitly refuse the old scalar RUN\nlane in a root-pinned launch. These constructor and lifetime observations\ndo not grant root-epoch authority, complete readiness, effects, capture,\nrestore or fork. Ordinary unpinned launches retain their existing behavior.\n\nRetain bounded native root epochs and exact held writer lifetimes.\n\nNegotiate dormant version-nine epoch registration without admitting native\nacquisition or effects. Preserve initialization ACK ownership, callback\nuserdata lifetime, original RUN transport and the default version-eight path.\n\nFence actual IRQ delivery and CPU source mutation before their first effects.\nBind original IRQ handles, callbacks and payloads; revalidate original CPU\nroster and retain sticky source divergence. Seal original endpoint inventories\nand refuse later block, character, network, monitor or iothread mutation.\n\nConfigured two-ISA source builds, existing native regressions and extracted\nproduction assertions pass for the exact reviewed components. Actual dormant\nconstruction and source-refusal probes preserve original custody. These\nchecks do not qualify RootSeal, a successful execution epoch, complete input\nor output closure, Ready, capture or fork. Ordinary disabled paths retain\nexisting behavior. Full registered-package qualification is separate.\n\nRetain finite original KVM service windows and canonical response bytes.\n\nKeep original CPU work out of ordinary drain paths. Bind the retained window,\npaused owner, callback generation, exit geometry and exact original response\nthrough Query, completion and acknowledgment. Interrupted or failed kernel\nreentry preserves sticky uncertainty; no callback is redispatched.\n\nPreserve all existing native construction, IRQ and endpoint guards and the\nlegacy KVM control encodings. New component namespaces refuse stopped TCG.\nFour new native implementation files carry explicit GPL-2.0-only notices.\nKernel response-stage inputs remain separate versioned source components.\n\nConfigured default two-ISA builds, native unit tests, existing source proofs\nand compiled adverse controls pass against the reviewed composition. These\ncomponents do not establish Ready, complete device or input/output closure,\nquantum execution, native snapshots or hardware qualification. Live KVM\nqualification remains outstanding on this machine without /dev/kvm.\n\nKeep the existing RR/Sim barrier extraction linked to its original producer.\n\nExtract the actual native-window work guard alongside queue_work_on_cpu.\nThe legacy-only fixture retains an explicitly disabled window generation and\nall original FIFO, BQL, timer, stop and healthy 8-to-3 cycle assertions.\nConfigured compilation and execution of nineteen existing source fixtures\npass; all five barrier defect controls compile and fail native assertions.\nNo production function, per-file license or qualification flag is changed.\n\nBind opted-in native effects to the original source factory, CPU owner,\nregistered endpoint roles and finite resource inventory. Retain exact\noriginal policy and handle identity through registration, epoch acquisition,\npartial CPU service and historical result recovery. Reject foreign threads,\ninherited processes, substituted handles and changed immutable policies.\n\nEnroll original QOM construction, memory dispatch and payload roots before\nsealed effect execution. Preserve default disabled paths and all current\nKVM source. Link the original installed endpoint owner through the production\nsystem Meson source set. Retain original IRQ payload checks and distinguish\nauthenticated startup exit acknowledgement from guest interrupt or work.\n\nThe retained configured prototype passes one actual instruction service and\nidentical result retry, together with real registration and process refusal\ncontrols. These component results do not establish completed grants, timer\ndispatch, output publication, interval parking, exact capture or Ready.\nThe current-parent production composition requires its matching full build,\nsource controls, corresponding source and post-plugin qualification.";
